    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "353d6dd1_f01a115b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-27T17:13:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that we\u0027re not behaving consistently with the expected USB-C analog behavior.  However, from talking to Jett we have two pretty good reasons for this: \n\n1. When a dongle presents Rd/Ra, presenting the 3.0 A Rp value can cause CCD mode detection, which in turn causes problems with HDMI working properly on the CCD port.  There was a CL 1121339 which covered most cases for this, but in the specific case of moving a plug from one port to the other, we can present 3.0 A Rp for about 30 ms, which triggers CCD and can cause dongles to not work (see b/123063171 for scope shots and details)\n\n2. When a bad analog port partner doesn\u0027t monitor the Rp value, they may see 3.0 A to start with and then continue drawing 3.0 A even after we\u0027ve set 1.5 A.  By starting at 1.5 A, a bad port port partner wouldn\u0027t draw more than this value even after Rp changes.",
      "parentUuid": "4da7045f_195d99c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "ece6ed9b0da60624cb39079e3dd7d5aed65a884e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c1f9514_707df9de",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-26T23:15:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the fact that the Rp-3.0A wasn\u0027t being consistently advertised, is a bug. However, now due to the false debug accessory detect, the Rp-3.0A is problematic.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "ece6ed9b0da60624cb39079e3dd7d5aed65a884e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6447f41b_9e875445",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-27T17:13:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes.  We\u0027ve discussed the CCD detection issue in b/124531988 if you\u0027d like to jump on that bug.  The general consensus is that we should be okay to present 3.0 A Rp after Vconn is applied.  Sine PD port partners are allowed to disregard the Rp value, this will only affect analog port partners.",
      "parentUuid": "9c1f9514_707df9de",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "ece6ed9b0da60624cb39079e3dd7d5aed65a884e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
